INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('homemade-airbrush-compressor', 'Sergej Voronko', 'I''m not sure if I got the question right but I''m sure nothing will happen if you turn it upside down. Just switch it off. And also if your compressor is refridgerator (pancake) type then you are risking losing the oil that is needed for its function. You have to empty the tank only.', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2013-08-21 12:33:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('homemade-airbrush-compressor', 'Alf Karlsson', 'hi Sergej i have a question the frees fluid that is left in the compressor is it OK to turn it upside down to empty that or will the oil also come out at the same time or is it enough to tilt  on the side so the frees fluid pore out i have not cut the oile pipe the compressor is one with out oilplug only a small pipe', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2013-08-17 15:18:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('homemade-airbrush-compressor', 'Sergej Voronko', 'No bother man, I''m happy that you''ve found something helpful here. I also recommend to check the other article too http://airbrushdoc.com/tipstricks/silent-compressor/', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2012-04-21 18:05:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('homemade-airbrush-compressor', 'Mayes1014', 'Been looking to build a silent compressor for a while now. Seen many guides but yours was the most helpful. Thank you for this.', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2012-04-21 16:02:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('homemade-airbrush-compressor', 'Sergej Voronko', 'Hi Per, I think you have not read this http://airbrushdoc.com/tipstricks/oil-compressor/, it is oil, not a gas, and I have replaced that mineral oil with half-synthetic one. Thanks for your concern anyway', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2012-02-10 23:13:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('homemade-airbrush-compressor', 'Per Jensen', 'I would personally recommend going to the local scrap yard and purchase a compressor that has already been reclaimed, for the scrap steel price. What do You mean by "still in the bottle" ? The refrigerant is a gas, and cannot be contained in any bottle, you need to pierce the copper tube with a special valve and by a pump transfer the gas to a holding pressure canister that can be processed accordingly. It sounds like you just have the oil from the compressor in a bottle, you should leave this in the compressor for lubrication, running it without oil is not good. Doing this is illegal in most of the world - its only up to the professionals to do this. So obtain a compressor from a scrap yard that is already taken out of the fridge.', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2012-02-10 18:56:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('homemade-airbrush-compressor', 'Sergej Voronko', 'Hi Per, I know about that but every country has different restriction about that. Do you have any recommendation?
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('homemade-airbrush-compressor', 'Per Jensen', 'I am a little concerned, when you tell people to just pull a compressor out of a fridge - do you know how harmfull the Freon or R134a is to the environment ? In most of the world, there is heavy fines if you get caught doing that. Freon destroys the ozone layer, and R134a is around 1400 times as harmful for the environment than CO2....', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2012-02-10 00:28:00');
