INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('paasche-big-name-in-airbrush-history', 'Donnie Fatten', 'Hello, 
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('paasche-big-name-in-airbrush-history', 'ken', 'Great story ... I''m an American who worked with airbrushes most of my artist life (I''m 73). In 1979 after 9 years with the Army I got an invitation to move Down Under (Australia) to teach airbrush techniques. In 1964 I bought my first airbrush a "Binks-Wren" (which I still have) for Automotive touch up as I was doing an apprenticeship as a bump and paint man ... back then you could attend High School from 7:05 AM to 11:55 AM and then work at the shop four hours, although my boss let us work longer hours and weekends if we wanted. I was paid $1.05 an hour. ...LOL. I went to college and never considered using an airbrush with my paintings. One teacher who did illustration work for GM, showed us his Paasche mdl H... I was hooked as he applied it doing washes over water color paintings in the sky or water without lifting any paint. I''ve done everything from fine art to catalog retouching machine parts, and even wedding photos.
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('paasche-big-name-in-airbrush-history', 'Tuck John Porter', 'Beautiful Paasche History Summary! Came here hunting the origin year date on the Paasche AB Turbo Air Gun. Nice to learn Mr. Paasche originally was working at Thayer & Chandler. My mom helped me buy an expensive Thayer & Chandler Air Gun my College Freshman Year in 1975. It was later stolen straight out of my Art building Locker. I purchased a Paasche VL Double Action Air Gun around 1978 and have used it ever since. What is your favorite Air Gun?', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2022-10-19 02:40:28');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('paasche-big-name-in-airbrush-history', 'R.T. Thomas', 'I was invited to my friend''s house this afternoon 11/23/2023 for an after Thanksgiving get together. We''ve been friends our whole lives. Our fathers grew up in the same small town together. Anyway, she married a guy from New England maybe New York) and they have been together for many years. I have never gotten to know him very well, but we talked quite a bit this afternoon and I mentioned that I have been an airbrush artist for about 40 years. He proceeded to tell that his great-great uncle was Jens Andreas Paasche!! I kinda freaked out. It was cool.', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2023-11-24 05:19:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('paasche-big-name-in-airbrush-history', 'Gail Glasier', 'Gail Glasier 928 715- 8805 has a model A Paasche with a receipt from 1941.', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2023-12-27 16:11:49');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('paasche-big-name-in-airbrush-history', 'Gail Glasier', 'Gail here again; correction on 1st post : I have a model B Paasche . The receipt has a signature of the artist that bought it from A. I. Friedman Artist and Draftsman Supplies. 43 West 47th st. New York. N.Y. Telephone ,Bryant 9- 4909. Artist name is; Pierre Mardrus his address is on next line as, 70 Paganr ( or is that an ''e'' ?) Ave. There are a few drawings and one ink work pieces of art listed for sale by Peirre , and the signatures are the same on receipt as on art !  It says he lived most of his life in California. I acquired the airbrush in about 1980ish in Laguna Beach .I used it a little until I bought an Aztec airbrush.', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2023-12-27 18:07:15');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('paasche-big-name-in-airbrush-history', 'airbrushdoc', 'what? this is unbelievable! :)', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2024-06-04 11:31:37');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('paasche-big-name-in-airbrush-history', 'Einar Ravndal', 'I''m not much of an airbrush man, but rather a humble history buff. Yesterday I read about the Nidaros Cathedral in Trondheim, Norway. It is the birthplace of your founder, Jens Andreas Paasche. On the top of the church is a bronze statue of St. Michael. It was given to the church by Jens Andreas Paasche, and put up in 1969. The sculptor, Kristofer Leirdal, opposed nuclear weapons and the Vietnam war. So, as his own little protest, he gave St. Michael the face of Bob Dylan. The story made me curious about what man Paasche was, and everything I know about you is what I found out during the last 24 hours. Impressing corporate story. Here''s a link to an English language page where you find the story: https://www.lifeinnorway.net/nidaros-cathedral/', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2025-12-08 10:13:01');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('permanent-or-temporary-3d-tattoo', 'Airbrush', 'Oh my God! These airbrush tattoos are so real. I just can not forget the one with spider on women''s shoulder. its spooky', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2011-11-05 13:31:00');
