INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Greg Lange', 'I represent a San Diego airbrush artist.  Some of his work is created by deep etching the image into a 24" round, 1/2" thick piece of glass or crystal.  He then comes in with the airbrush, and adds color creating a beautiful piece.  This is a rare medium.  Has anyone attempted this method?  Results?  What do you think of his work?', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2014-06-13 16:48:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Merlin Lenchanteur', 'i i had start with a veda 180 on ebay for 45$ witch have air regulation same as iwate hp-ch (the one i would like) i had buy it with a free gift, nozzle and needle in 0.2 and in 0.3. i had try some paint into it too (golden, createx, wicked, fast color and yes... dolorama lol) the best one is wicked in 0.2. (my 0.3 never work fine... ), its the only one i can reduce enought to use the 0.2 mmm and have a great result but i have the problem too with the centering of the nozzle. i turn it to center as maximum before use ... 6 mnounth and he ad lost a lot of precision . now i dont want to paint anything with it its just to hard beacause now i can use it with some skill... i had buy a veda 130 )for 20$ ! (without air regulation) on ebay but this one doesn''t work att all lol i had take some part on them lol now to continue to learn i think ill need a bether one like de hp-ch... i had read on the internet, de master and the veda are really same for the quality. but... with all the chineese copy, one can work and the second no... if you have chance you will have a good one like me in the first time :) 
(the paint is on a 8.5" x 11 " inch sheet)', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2014-03-22 23:38:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'merlin l''enchanteur', 'i i had start with a veda 180 on ebay for 45$ witch have air regulation same as iwate hp-ch (the one i would like) i had buy it with a free gift, nozzle and needle in 0.2 and in 0.3. i had try some paint into it too (golden, createx, wicked, fast color and yes... dolorama lol) the best one is wicked in 0.2. (my 0.3 never work fine... ), its the only one i can reduce enought to use the 0.2 mmm and have a great result but i have the problem too with the centering of the nozzle. i turn it to center as maximum before use ... 6 mnounth and he and it lost a lot of precision . now i dont want to paint anything with it its just to much hard beacause now i can use it with some skill... i had buy a veda 130 )for 20$ ! (without air regulation) on ebay too but this one doesn''t work att all lol i had take some part on them lol now to continue to learn i think ill need a bether one like de hp-ch... i had read on the internet, de master and the veda are really same for the quality. but... with all the chineese copy, one can work and the second no... if you have chance you will have a good one like me the first time :) look what was my second airbrush ever with this :) (8.5"x11"sheet)', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2014-03-22 23:32:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Sergej Voronko', 'Thanks for this detailed description man. I really appreciate it and I think you''ve got the point.
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'shadow_rider', 'Sorry, I forgot to answer your thinner question.....these are water based paints and I only thin with water but clean with a 50/50 solution of windex in a ultrasonic cleaner. if I feel I need something stronger I use a few drops of valejo thinner. BTW, the windex I use contains NO ammonia, NO vinegar, and NO phosphates, I get it at Sam''s Club in the gallon size jugs for $4', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2013-07-13 09:44:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'serzomanik', 'Hey Megan, no I never have heard about Veda but I certainly going to check them out.', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2012-04-11 08:19:40');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'shadow_rider', 'Trust me, I am not by any means trying to say a person shouldn''t purchase a high end brush, I am just trying to say that I feel something like a Masters series could be a very good entry level machine if you are on a budget. As for the paint I use...currently I am using Valejo because it is redily available at my local hobby shop but do intend to try create, especially the Wicked and AutoAir lines because I want to get into doing some art on my truck and my sons bike. I started with a cheapo $15 airbrush from harbor freight and moved up to Masters currently. Will I purchase an Iwatta, or a Badger in the future, probably but my point was most people cant afford to lay out $200 - $500 just starting out so while I do agree from a professional level a masters wouldn''t work for Ed Hubbs, or Mike Lavelle, or any other pro brusher, I feel should guide people to what they are comfortable with. In my humble opinion I feel something like a Master series would be an acceptable entry level brush. 
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Sergej Voronko', 'Hey Shadow_rider!
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'shadow_rider', 'I own a Masters MAS 233 set, has .2, .3, and .5 needles and tips. Cost was $60 US and works flawlessly for me. I understand steering people towards the higher end brushes but I feel it is a bit unfair to be condemned so easily. Realistically, your not comparing apples to apples its like buying little ole granny a 100k sports car who only drives once a week...its just not practical. Speaking for myself, you can give anyone all the tools they could ever want or need but if they don''t take the time to learn how to use them ... it was all for nothing. JMHO', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2013-07-13 00:30:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Sergej Voronko', 'Hi Todd,
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Todd', 'Great topic we have a box of 3 china airbrush''s , we bought a airbrush off a guy that we knew with compressor it blew about 8 lbs of air with a airbrush that was a miss mash of parts it was branded buy a store which is out of biz go figure.  We then bought 3 more china brush''s which all broke with in a week or 2 ya I know dumb dumb the cost of a education I guess at least we can use the old needles to clean our good airbrush''s right?
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Mark', 'Hi, I''m frustrated...got a g22. Its new and clogging up. I tried pressure 20 and I''m unsure about reducer consistency in paint. Any advise?', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2013-02-13 01:07:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Sergej Voronko', 'My only advice here is to make paint thin like milk, if this does not help then make it even thinner. And also clean that airbrush properly. Some time it may start clogging because you use fast drying reducer...', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2013-02-13 05:59:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Sergej Voronko', 'Hey man, for your problem there are many different solutions. It depends on the other factors then airbrush itself. I would like to know what paint are you using (too big pigments in paint ca cause the problem). If you can buy an ink refills for ink-jet printer, try it. Ink has very soft pigments that will go trough any size of a nozzle. It will mean that you are not using the right paint. If ink won''t come out then I would take the brush apart and check bearings.
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'dissappointed', 'I have Master airbrush, as seen in your picture, It is brand new, my second one the first one the paint didn''t come out, they had me throw it away, sent me another one, it still don''t work.  The paint will not come out!!   It does Spray water though!', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2012-10-19 19:22:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Sergej Voronko', 'Hey Tim, I probably don''t really understand, is that bear a fiberglass sculpture? If yes, I think you can go wrong with Iwata. For stencils I am not sure, I don''t have experience with 3D forms but you can check ORAMASK 810 http://www.oracal.com/products/product.asp?seriesID=186', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2012-04-28 10:58:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Tim', 'Some years ago I airbrushed T-shirts and Tags at a local market during the summers. I am preparing to participate in a community project . I will be painted a lifesize fiberglass bear. I will need to use an automotive paint and will be spraying shapes in the 1"4 to 3" sized round and ovaltype shapes. I''m thinking an Iwata that holds the paint in a bottle. Any suggestions would be appreciated. I could also use advise on stencil material for painting this  3 dimensional form.', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2012-04-27 15:58:00');
INSERT INTO comments (slug, author, body, status, ip_hash, created_at) VALUES ('master-airbrush-review', 'Megan', 'Do you know anything about "Veda" airbrushed.  It''s another cheapo brand like the master but wasn''t sure if they had the same issues or If it was at least a good enough brush for beginners to learn on before deciding on the better well known named brushes.  Thanks!', 'approved', 'wp-import', '2012-04-11 05:12:00');
